erlandt 1984), and Caucasian Region and Central Asia including, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Georgia, Iran, Kazakhstan, Kirgizia, Tadjikistan, Uzbekistan. Host plants. On Triticum sp. (Poaceae) (Modarres Awal 1996 a, 1997 a, b; Khanjani 2006), Tamarix sp. (Tamaricaceae) (Modarres Awal 1997 b), wild Poaceae (Modarres Awal 1996 a; Linnavuori 2008; Nateq Golestan et al. 2011), Brachiaria eruciformis (Poaceae), Trifolium sp. (Fabaceae) (Sakenin et al. 2008), Atriplex sp. (Amaranthaceae) and Hordeum vulgare (Poaceae) (Nateq Golestan & Modarres Awal 2012). It has been mentioned on several other Poaceae such as Agropyrum caespitosum, A. pectiniforme, Alopecurus arundinaceus, Arrhenatherum kotchsyi, Boisseria squarrosa, Bromus lanceolatus (Derjanschi & Péricart 2005).","","text","",""]]},"LBKPX":{"d":[["Global","","text","native","least concern"]]},"LBZRG":{"d":[["Distribution. India (West Bengal), Nepal.","","text","",""]]},"LJK9G":{"d":[["Distribution. China: Gansu, Shaanxi.","","text","",""]]},"LNDC":{"d":[["Bolivia (La Paz)","","text","",""]]},"M54K":{"d":[["Ecuador","","text","native",""]]},"N595P":{"d":[["ISO 3166-2:CA-BC","","text","native",""],["ISO 3166-2:US-AK","","text","native",""]]},"N94RT":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"N9523":{"d":[["Sweden","SE","iso","",""]]},"PFHC":{"d":[["","MOL","tdwg","",""]]},"PW3QV":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","",""]]},"PXNX3":{"d":[["Distribution. North America (USA and Canada), Northern Asia westward to the Yamal peninsula (north of Western Siberia). Zemskaya (1973) mentioned L. alaskensis from Komi Republic of Russia situated in the northeast corner of East Europe.","","text","",""]]},"PYP26":{"d":[["Distribution: Brazil (Minas Gerais and São Paulo).","","text","",""]]},"QMGCY":{"d":[["ISO 3166-2:CA-AB","","text","native",""],["ISO 3166-2:CA-NB","","text","native",""],["ISO 3166-2:CA-QC","","text","native",""]]},"QNTN":{"d":[["New Guinea (Papua New Guinea)","","text","",""]]},"R5DV":{"d":[["BOR-SB","BOR-SB","tdwg","",""],["SUM","SUM",